sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-27> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The normal curve of growth of an organism closely resembles the velocity curve of an autocatalytic chemical reaction, with a phase of increasing acceleration, a phase in which limiting conditions reduce acceleration, and usually a final phase of retardation and loss of mass; but only a resemblance, not an identity, can yet be asserted.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The organic curve of growth resembles the velocity curve of chemical autocatalysis";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter III, “The Rate of Growth”; topic “Growth and catalytic action”. Scope: growth of organisms generally"
}
